---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content } from '../content/corpus/columna_thesis_v0_4.md';
import TermChipStrip from '../components/TermChipStrip.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="The Columna Thesis — datumwise"
  description="The Columna Thesis (v0.7) — a dated position piece, reproduced as written.">
  {/* STANDING, NOT A REWRITE (Huayin, 2026-08-27, positioning repair §4). The essay below is a
      frozen corpus edition and its bytes may not be edited. It argues from the launch-era framing
      and contains sentences — "Columna is our proof that the discipline can be made executable" —
      that read as current positioning when the page gives them no date. The repair is chrome only:
      say what edition this is and when it was written, and let the argument stand as written. */}
  <p class="standing wayfinding">
    <span class="standing-mark mono">edition</span>
    <span>The Columna Thesis, <strong>v0.7</strong> — reproduced here as written. It is a dated
    position piece, not a current statement of what datumwise or Columna is; for that, see
    <a href="/about">About</a> and <a href="/columna">Columna</a>.</span>
  </p>
  <article class="prose">
    <Content />
  </article>
  <p class="engage wayfinding">
    This is a thesis, not a petition. Dispute it, extend it, or bring evidence —
    <a href="https://github.com/datumwise/columna/discussions" rel="noopener" target="_blank">in the open</a>.
    Shorter, with two live exhibits: <a href="/the-argument">the argument</a>.
  </p>
  <TermChipStrip />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .standing { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: baseline; margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .standing-mark { font-size: 0.68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--ink-faint); white-space: nowrap; }
  .standing a { color: var(--ink); }

  .engage { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
